hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24341","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abu Ammar, who said: I asked Qays ibn Sa'd about the charity of breaking the fast, and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us before zakat was revealed, then zakat was revealed, and we were neither forbidden it nor commanded it, and we do it, and I asked him about the fast of Ashura, and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us before Ramadan was revealed, then Ramadan was revealed, and we were neither commanded it nor forbidden it, and we do it."
"24342","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, that Qays ibn Sa'd ibn Ubadah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever strengthens his authority through disobedience to Allah, Allah will weaken his plot on the Day of Resurrection."
"24343","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, and Muhammad ibn Ja'far, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Ibn Abi Layla, that Sahl ibn Hunayf and Qays ibn Sa'd were sitting at al-Qadisiyyah, and a funeral passed by, so they stood, and it was said: It is only one of the people of the land, so they said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had a funeral pass by him and he stood, and it was said to him: He is a Jew, so he said: Is it not a soul."
"24344","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abu Ammar al-Hamdani, from Qays ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us with the charity of breaking the fast before zakat was revealed, then when zakat was revealed, he neither commanded us nor forbade us, and we do it."
"24345","Waki' narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd ibn Zurarah, from Muhammad ibn Shurahbil, from Qays ibn Sa'd, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us, and we placed washing water for him and he bathed, then we brought him a dyed sheet of wars and he wrapped himself in it, and it is as if I look at the trace of the wars upon his flanks, then we brought him a donkey to ride, and the owner of the donkey said: The owner of the donkey is most entitled to the front of his donkey, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, then the donkey is yours."
